# First CTF04 assembly ingress proposal

SOURCE ONLY. This is an API/owner plan for Header's future reviewed proposal,
not an implemented cache owner, retry driver, comparison, or gate result.

Reuse the actual current ConstructionCtfInitialDiscretization and the exact
ConstructionCtfLayerPreprocessing that fed it. A small public initializer may
take only references to these two existing owners and return an ordered
ConstructionCtfFirstAssembly { construction_id, result } owner. Its Result
must preserve explicit InitialUnavailable(CtfInitialUnavailable), missing
PostConversion, association/caller-owner mismatch, and AssemblyScope errors.
The existing InitialUnavailable route must remain distinct; no fake matrix
or default context is supplied for unused/error/allR/reverse/scope stops.

Only an actual initial.result Ok with the same construction ID and genuine
preprocessing.result/after_conversion may invoke the accepted pure assembly.
Borrow converted.active.layers. Copy Nodes/dx from initial.active into local
temporary slices without arithmetic. Copy rcmax, NodeSource, NodeUserTemp,
initial_ctf_time_step_hours and initial_num_histories from that same Result.
Use the same initial wrapper's real context and time_step_zone_hours; require
the initial result's caller copy to match, without deriving a replacement.
No node placement, spacing, resistance, reverse classification or timestep
selection is repeated by the adapter.

The selected adapter actually calls assemble_1d_ctf_state_space once with
route Assemble and attempt_ordinal 1. This ordinal records that real first
Rust assembly invocation, not evidence of a Native or Rust retry loop. The
accepted pure function initializes actual AMat/IdenMatrix and compressed
B3/C2/D2 using unchanged source arithmetic. Nonfinite returned arithmetic
retains its real class; missing and nonfinite owners are different concepts.

Production cache integration should construct the new owner immediately after
its existing initial owner, using the same entry.ctf01_layer_preprocessing,
then retain an ordered parallel Vec and expose it through HeatBalanceState.
The existing CTF01 preprocessing, CTF02 coefficient storage/cache hash and
CTF03 initial owner are unchanged. Unit observations call the same adapter
on genuine literal-derived typed owners; production observations borrow the
actual ordinary initialized cache owner. Observers never assemble matrices.

All actual Native assembly attempts must remain separately observed. Only
the first may be paired with this actual Rust owner until the genuine CTF05-08
solver/retry driver exists. Never inject later Native CTFTimeStep/NumHistories
into Rust or relabel a final whole-return snapshot as initial state. This API
does not call exponential/inverse/Gamma/final coefficients or modify old
massive fallback behavior. Header/Root settle the concrete typed API before
source implementation; no additional QA execution stage is introduced.
